function Get-ProcessReport {
  param($Name)
  $out = @()
  Get-Process | Where-Object { $_.Name -like $Name } | ForEach-Object {
    $out += [pscustomobject]@{ Name = $_.Name; CPU = $_.CPU; WS = $_.WS }
  }
  $out | Sort-Object CPU -Descending
}

Rewrite Get-ProcessReport for PowerShell 7. Use [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess)], typed params, begin/process/end, ValueFromPipeline, ForEach-Object -Parallel for the process walk, and no += on arrays. Output only the revised function.
